    "notes": "Tuned empirically for WheelModified.stl (498x498x84 mm, 2.56 L solid, 2.15 M triangles) - mock-up only, no strength required. Measured on this part: supports are ~59% of all extruded material, so the support settings are the main lever, not the part settings. Verified better than the alternatives: tree/organic supports were WORSE here (3d18h vs 1d14h); flipping the part 180 deg cut geometric overhang 35% but gained only ~4% real time while losing a third of the bed contact - so print it as-is, flat. 1 wall + 2/1 shells is deliberate: fine for a mock-up, do NOT reuse for functional parts. Brim is essential: only ~205 cm2 of a ~1960 cm2 circle touches the bed. TRAVEL SPEED: capped at 150 mm/s deliberately. CoreXY drives one motor at v*sqrt(2) on a 45-degree move, and the firmware's per-actuator ceiling is 316.7 mm/s (alpha/beta_max_rate 19000 mm/min) - so any travel above 224 mm/s overruns a motor on diagonals. An earlier 250 mm/s setting caused a real print failure: cumulative diagonal layer shift. Raise only after testing, and never above 224.",
